  "step_1": "The decision reason specifies a method for evaluating lotteries based on identifying the 'sure outcome' — the outcome with the minimum absolute value (which in both lotteries is 0 Euros). Then, it computes the differences between the sure outcome (0) and the other outcomes (4000€ and 3000€), and evaluates the weighted sum of these differences using their probabilities. The reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable weighted sum of (sure outcome + differences). In this case:\n\n- For Lottery A: Sure outcome = 0€ (with 80% probability), difference = 4000€ - 0 = 4000€, probability = 20%. Weighted difference = 4000€ × 0.20 = 800€.\n- For Lottery B: Sure outcome = 0€ (with 75% probability), difference = 3000€ - 0 = 3000€, probability = 25%. Weighted difference = 3000€ × 0.25 = 750€.\n\nThe weighted sum of differences is higher for A (800€) than for B (750€), so the reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the decision reason is applicable and can be evaluated in this problem.",
